  Parity reproduced from the web source (every REAL branch — no fabricated chrome):
   - optional Display-Mode grid (showMode): 7 modes, icon + name + 4 bg->surface swatches + checkmark
   - always-present Accent-Colour grid: 5 presets (gradient primary->accent) + selected checkmark
   - optional Custom swatch (showCustom) sourced from live custom colours
   - Custom RGB builder (showCustom && themeId==custom): Primary/Accent native colour wells + live hex
   - compact vs full layout (web `compact`)
   - toast.info("Theme: <name>") / ("Mode: <name>") on a pick (web handleTheme/handleMode/handleCustom)
   - onChange / onModeChange callbacks; once-only view.opened (P1/S11)
   - native "never a blank box" empty leaf for a degenerate store (no themes)
  Faithful-parity note: the web <ThemePicker> is a PURELY presentational settings control (hooks:
  useTranslation/useToast/useTheme; NO fetcher). It therefore has NO loading/error/stale/offline async
  branch — reproducing the source's real branches only, the same precedent as siblings Accordion(0203)
  & CopyButton(0207). Inventing async chrome would fabricate states the source does not have.

